These can be very convenient places, especially in the early game as
that gold can be used to buy intrinsice protection from the Minetown
Priest, but I digress...

These rooms are not too challenging but it's nice to keep the majority
of them asleep otherwise they end up all over the level.  AFAIK, if you
don't set off any explosions (exploding traps on containers or boxes,
landmines, exploding spheres, etc.) or kick any doors on the level the
ones that have not been attacked will stay asleep.  I don't know if
stealth is required to not wake them, maybe someone else can comment on
that?  Generally it is nice to kill them quickly as they often have
handy magic items (potions of *foo*healing, scrolls of teleport, wands
of digging, etc.) that they will use up once their hp get too low.
Generally I just melee them one at a time as they don't seem to be too
worthy of much else but I do have a hard time killing each quickly as
they have a LVL=5.

If you have a tinning kit these can be convenient one stop shops for
gaining teleportitis (if you're into that sort of thing).
Incidentally, carnivorous pets do eat leprechauns.

Leprechauns will steal gold from your main inventory and then teleport
away if you have gold in your main inventory or are standing on gold,
so unless you want them to leave you alone for a while make sure that
your gold is either stashed in a container or dropped somewhere other
than where you are standing.  

